# Inert803 trusted scalar dependency discovery

Based on unacceptedStageBf41d6b5; no visibility/owner-current/public projection/registry activation. New private helper accepts selected claim/retraction/resolution IDs, strict positive ints/no duplicates/100 combined. Derives ONLY own record.evidence and scope (retraction via claim), never original claim evidence, automatic scope evidence or resolution claim_ids. Same-case exact found sets required.
One DISTINCT scope union covers initial scopes plus all four native evidence link types; all historical claim templates included, even retracted. No recursive evidence expansion, no Finance/leadership/version/binding discovery. No definition/body/note payload reads. Native base active case/document/policy reader gates and current default RR marker required; marker and returned closure are NOT authority. Topology is private frozen dataclass, no public serializer/visibility boolean.
Separate ScalarClosureBudget is tied to entry token and underlying default connection, not JSON byte-cell accounting. Per-operation distinct selected records<=100, own evidence<=100, relevant scopes<=100, templates<=100 and total identities<=400. Repeated identities free only in same entry; four edge paths share scope budget. DB joins can still scan many rows; not query-time/RSS bound. Overflow aborts without successful closure; no unrelated-case cap.
Four pure checks pass normal/-O; five native definitions discovered DB-forbidden/static, all UNRUN. Native definitions cover each seedkind, retracted template retention, shared scope/cap and missing record. Still UNPROVEN: full four-edge aggregate boundary, foreign template/source negative, reader revocation, actual SQL no-hydration instrumentation, concurrent RR closure append, integration rollback. These must precede activation. No DB or production flow changes. Existing StageA/StageB/snapshot and805/old803 branches preserved.

## Additional source-only definitions and entry hardening
Ten scalar native definitions now include distinct native scopes reached independently by all four evidence edges, exact five-scope admission and artificial cap4 overflow (not a100-scope stress proof); foreign selected record exclusion under another legitimate case; document-reader revocation/inactive entry before domain queries; absent/expired/cross-entry budget; captured SQL column exclusion for body/note/definition/claim_ids. All remain UNRUN. Foreign evidence/template corruption is NOT fabricated to bypass native constraints; those found-set defense branches remain without negative native proof. Concurrent append and integrated rollback also remain pending.
Snapshot marker now binds the exact freshly reloaded callback user object AND original pk. StageB and scalar discovery require that identity before their first ORM/native gate query. Original pre-entry user, another instance with same pk, different user and mutated pk are rejected. Native grants still mandatory; trusted callbacks must not mutate other principal state. This is accident prevention, not a hostile-Python security boundary or through-commit revocation guarantee. No production wiring.

## Two-connection definitions (UNRUN)
Two additional definitions in test_template_scalar_snapshot803 use a real separate bounded writer connection/backend PID. Native register_scope commits a relevant own-evidence link: the established RR entry must retain its closure and the next entry must see the new scope. Native intake.provision establishes narrowly synthetic technical document.read management (local test superuser bootstrap, no business owner role); native change_access revokes the grant: established RR still observes prior authorization, next entry denies before domain queries. This explicitly demonstrates snapshot-time observation, NOT authorization through commit or approval of that production contract.
Worker native scope/revision/Audit or authority/AccessChange/Grant/Audit changes are deliberate fixture effects, not no-effect projection. These require explicit future runtime scope. Workers use separate connections,2s lock/5s statement timeouts,10s bounded joins, exception propagation and finally-close; no surviving worker can count success. No retries or DB guard bypass. Three static pure tests inspect definitions; actual concurrency, native bootstrap, scheduling and cleanup remain UNRUN. No route/registry/adapter activation.

## Entry-shared scalar identity and work limits (source only)
ScalarClosureBudget now requires the fresh callback actor plus exact entry keys. One marker-owned ledger shares identities and phase attempts across every wrapper, bound to original actor object/pk, normalized keys, default connection/raw connection and marker. Fixed identity caps unchanged: selected records100 combined across three kinds, evidence100, scopes100, templates100, total400. Six closed kind labels; strict positive integer validation occurs before dedup (including mixed1/True rejection). Returned identity view is immutable; no decoded payload or byte charging added.
A separate1000 scalar-phase cap debits before each discovery ORM evaluation and each of three native reader-gate invocations. One successful discovery uses12–14 permits depending on1–3 selected record kinds. Repeated same identities still spend phase permits; wrappers cannot reset them. Native gate invocation may issue internal queries: this is NOT a cap on allSQL, DB scans/CPU, policy/other-domain cell work or memory. Existing seed graph, same-case sets, four-edge DISTINCT union, all historical templates and native predicates remain unchanged; no new consumers wired.
Selection/preflight, context, constructor, query, native grant and cap failures poison original/current recognized entry fence, retaining charges without retry/refund. Existing snapshot exit guard rejects a caught failure before returning a prior result; no entry implementation changes. Native tests now expect this stronger exit failure after intentionally caught discovery errors. Their signatures use the fresh actor; all remain UNRUN. No DB/native fixture executed.
Ten isolated new pure tests plus four existing closure and three snapshot-definition tests pass normally and optimized. Tests cover shared identity/phase boundaries, pre-dedup strictness, both-entry poisoning, actor/pk/rawconnection changes, constructor/preflight failures and immutable views. They do not prove actual SQL/concurrency/rollback. Frozen395, policy/Finance/PMO readers and backup files are untouched by this increment.
